.S. Senate Race", "source": "UMass Lowell", "published": "2026-09-24T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMieEFVX3lxTFA3bjM5RWY0ekR6Z01IUXZta2xYVmxZeUlnTDUtblNCRUVDLVlROEZYRGpfREM1UGhYY1BmeW1HeldOSExIWjRHcWtqTDB3QU9taTVUVTk2Z1RFWGtqYUx4X0U3N2I3NVZvOFI2dUllcW12UEtIdXpmcQ?oc=5"}, {"title": "Hannah Pingree leads fundraising in Maine’s race for governor", "source": "Bangor Daily News", "published": "2026-09-24T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiugFBVV95cUxOQ0xyVnR5dmRoVkpYWExQVWVyYk1vcXdBd2c0d25rcHJBcVdHUFp5WEx2SFIzYk81NzROREhkdVBZMkVObFN1ZDNqRWFlUkd5SVlOY2Fpbll5VGlGSXc1X1I2elQzUHRvQ18tRG90LU5IQnhlejJ1bVd0ZDVJU05BbnphRHBhbGJkZTZRTE9haTNXeWJzbnpPLXJwWmlXdkgwWm5ISkQzcWIyLXAtVGdEVDdDOHhYNllib2c?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": 10.83, "prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 11.6, "poll_sd": 4.52, "poll_weight": 0.58, "fundamentals": {"margin": 7.58, "lean": 3.0, "environment": 4.2, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": 0.38}, "rating_margin": 13.0, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.46, "baseline_margin": 11.28, "analyst_adjustment": 0.22, "key_factors": ["Consistent double-digit polling lead for Pingree across 13 surveys", "Strong Democratic fundamentals in Maine plus open-seat continuity from Mills", "Pingree's fundraising edge and unified expert ratings of Likely/Solid D", "Independent Rick Bennett may siphon votes but mostly from the right lane"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Pingree ahead by 9 to 12 points, and markets price her near 95% to win. With solid ratings from most analysts and a clear money advantage, the race sits comfortably in Safe D territory despite the open seat.", "watch": "A late debate-driven shift or Bennett consolidating anti-Pingree voters could narrow the margin, though a genuine upset would require a major polling miss.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Janet Mills (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Maine's open governor's race features Democrat Hannah Pingree against Republican Bobby Charles, with independent Rick Bennett also on the ballot. Term-limited incumbent Janet Mills leaves the seat to a Democratic-leaning state with a partisan lean of about four points Democratic.\n\nPolling has been remarkably consistent: thirteen surveys since mid-August all show Pingree ahead, with recent high-quality polls from Marist, CBS/YouGov, and the Washington Post putting her lead between 9 and 13 points. Pingree has outraised Charles roughly two to one and holds a cash advantage. Expert raters uniformly call the race Likely or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets price her win probability around 95%. The main residual uncertainty is the size of the margin rather than the outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9699, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9727, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9762, "margin": 11.5}]}